.\" link.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX link(1) utility, which this
.\" tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/LINK.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/LINK.
.TH LINK 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
link \- call the link function
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Link
is not provided on maux.
ProDOS has no hard links, no symbolic links, and no named pipes
(docs/ANACHRONISMS.md sec W2).
